而现在我觉得，这既是对那段历史的回顾，同时这也预示了——坦率地说——20世纪俄罗斯历史上的许多主题：作秀审判、怀疑、偏执、对内部敌人的执着搜寻。因为彼得显然（考虑到他的童年，我猜这是可以理解的）对针对他的阴谋这一概念有着病态的执念。如果没有这样一个阴谋，他甚至会觉得有必要捏造一个，因为必须得有这么个阴谋。所以在这次盛大集会几天后，他对阿列克谢说，我需要你把所有跟你谈过我们关系的人的名字都列出来。

90
00:43:25.000 --> 00:44:05.000
And now I think this, it looks back to that, but also so many of the themes of this anticipate frankly 20th century Russian history, show trials, suspicion, paranoia, an obsessive search for enemies within. Because Peter is clearly, I guess for understandable reasons, given his boyhood, he is obsessed with the idea of a conspiracy against him. And if there isn't one, he almost feels the need to invent it because there must be one. So a few days after this great sort of assembly, he says to Alexis, I need you to list for me everybody you've ever spoken to about our relationship.
而阿列克谢完全听信了这话，开出了一份长长的名单，上面列满了亲戚、朝臣、朋友和家庭教师。彼得一拿到这份名单，立刻给圣彼得堡的亚历山大·缅什科夫下达命令：关上城门，封锁全城，然后派你的特工去把名单上的每一个人都给我抓起来。也就是说，包括贵族、主教、军官，还有阿列克谢所有的前仆人。我们要对他们所有人进行审讯，把这个阴谋查个水落石出。名单上的其中一个人是阿列克谢的母亲、彼得的前妻叶夫多基娅。所以她还在世。

91
00:44:05.000 --> 00:44:43.000
And Alexis, who is completely gullible, produces this huge list of relatives and courtiers and friends and tutors and as soon as Peter has the list in his hands, he sends orders to Alexander Menshikov in St Petersburg, close the gates and seal off the city and now send your agents out to round up every single person on this list. So that's aristocrats, it's bishops, it's officers, all Alexis's former servants. We're going to interrogate them all and get to the bottom of this conspiracy. Now one of the people on this list is Alexis's mother, Peter's ex-wife Eudokia. So she's still around.
她过去19年一直待在苏兹达尔的修道院里。但她一直在给阿列克谢写信，更糟糕的是彼得早把她给忘了。但当他的特工赶到时，他们发现她已经不再当修女了。哦，所以她的头发又长出来了。她的头发长回来了，不仅如此，她还开始谈恋爱了，对象是她卫队的队长——本该负责看守她的人，一个名叫斯捷潘·格列博夫的男子。于是彼得说，什么？他下令逮捕了格列博夫，还有修道院院长和一些修女。

92
00:44:43.000 --> 00:45:15.000
She's been in the monastery in Suzdal for the last 19 years But she has been writing to Alexis and there is worse Peter just forgotten about her. But when his agents arrived they find she's given up being a nun Oh, so she's growing her hair back. Her hair has returned and what is more? She has been living in a relationship With the captain of her guards the man who's meant to to be guarding her is a man called Stepan Glebov. And so Peter says, what? And he has Glebov arrested as well as the head of the convent and some of the nuns.
多米尼克，我可不想成为格列博夫。你绝对不会想的，原因接下来就会变得显而易见。于是他们开始进行作秀审判。这些审判在克里姆林宫的大厅里举行。彼得亲自担任首席检察官，他对名单上的所有人提出了指控。以修道院里的叶夫多基娅为例，那些什么都没做的修女们被判处公开鞭笞。叶夫多基娅被送到北方一个真正偏远的修道院，但其他一些囚犯则被判处死刑、用九尾鞭毒打或流放。

93
00:45:15.000 --> 00:45:53.000
Dominic, I would not want to be in Glebov's boots. You absolutely would not for reasons that will now become apparent. So now they begin the show trials. These are held in the great hall of the Kremlin. Peter himself acts as chief prosecutor and he makes the case against all of the names on this list. To give the example of Eudokia in the convent, the nuns who have done nothing are sentenced to be publicly flogged. Eudokia is sent to a really remote convent up in the north, but some of the other prisoners are sentenced to death or beaten with a knout or exiled.
因为哪个法官能经受得住检察官的上诉诱惑，如果这个检察官就是沙皇本人呢？完全正确。所以许多判刑都是在红场执行的。我的意思是，这真是彼得大帝标志性的残暴作风：用铁锤把人的骨头砸碎，割掉鼻子，拔掉舌头。但最糟糕的命运留给了这个家伙——看守叶夫多基娅的卫队队长斯捷潘·格列博夫。记住，他其实什么坏事都没做。好吧，他跟彼得的前妻睡了，但那是他的前妻。我可不会去跟彼得大帝的前妻睡觉。对，这倒也是。好吧，我的意思是，你可不想落得这般下场。于是，格列博夫被九尾鞭狠狠抽打，并用烧红的铁块烙烫。他被绑在一块钉满尖刺的木板上，就这样被晾在那里三天，他们不断地对他说，招供吧。而他说，招供什么？我又从来没有参与过什么阴谋。最后，他们把格列博夫抬起来，把他穿在一根木桩上。有些记载说这木桩插得极其巧妙，竟然避开了他身上所有的要害器官，然后他就被留在这根木桩上慢慢下沉——我不知道如果一个人被穿在木桩上会发生什么——他花了14个小时才死去。天哪。我的意思是，可能确实有更残酷的死法，但我实在想不出几个了。

94
00:45:53.000 --> 00:46:28.000
Because what judge can resist the appeal of the prosecutor if the prosecutor is the Tsar? Exactly. So a lot of the sentences were carried out in Red Square. I mean, it's the classic, you know, Peter the Great carry on of people being broken with hammers on the wheel, people having their noses sliced off, having their tongues ripped out. But the worst fate of all is reserved for this bloke, Stepan Glebov, the captain of the guards, guarding Eudokia. And remember, he has done nothing wrong. Well, he has slept with Peter's ex-wife, but she's his ex-wife. I wouldn't sleep with Peter the Great's ex-wife. No, fair enough. Well, I mean, you don't want to end up like this. So, Glebov is lashed with the knout and he's burned
没有。尽管他没有找到任何阴谋的证据，但彼得从来没有想过其实根本没有什么阴谋，而且他手下的走狗没有一个敢跟他争辩这件事。否则他们就会招致怀疑。完全正确。这让人非常强烈地联想到20世纪30年代的斯大林，因为你该如何证明自己清白，去对抗一个根本不存在的阴谋呢？至于阿列克谢，他在这个时候大概能期盼的最好结果就是被流放到

95
00:46:28.000 --> 00:47:06.000
with red hot irons. He's stretched out on a plank with spikes driven into his flesh and left there for three days and they keep saying to him, confess. And he says, confess what? Like, I was never part of any conspiracy. And finally, they take Lebov and they impale him on a wooden stake which some accounts say was so artfully inserted that it missed all his vital organs and then he's left on this stake to sort of slowly descend I suppose, I don't know what happens to you if you're impaled on a stake, and it took him 14 hours to die. Oh God. I mean there may well be grimmer ways to die, but I can't think of many.
修道院去。但当然，如果彼得坚信他真的是某个阴谋的核心，那么潜台词就是这个阴谋还会继续，即使他在修道院里，他也将成为阴谋和反对势力的焦点。因此目前彼得将他软禁在圣彼得堡，而可怜的阿列克谢——这个如此悲剧性的人物，又是如此地自己坑自己——一直在苦苦哀求。求求你们。我能见见阿弗罗西尼娅吗？你答应过我可以和她一起生活的，我太爱她了。

96
00:47:06.000 --> 00:47:31.000
No. And even though he's found no evidence of the conspiracy, Peter, it never occurs to him that there isn't one and none of his henchmen ever argue with him about it. Then they would come under suspicion. Exactly. It feels very much reminiscent of Stalin in the 1930s because how can you prove your innocence of a conspiracy that never actually existed? Now as for Alexis, the best that he can probably hope for at this point is to be exiled to
最后她被带到首都接受审讯，一切对阿列克谢来说都急转直下。她支持他吗？她没有，汤姆。她没有。她没有支持自己的男人。因此，在她的行李中，彼得的特工发现了阿列克谢写给俄罗斯各路权贵的信件草稿，信中抱怨了他所受到的虐待。彼得亲自审问了阿弗罗西尼娅，他把她带来见自己，坐下来盘问她，这对她来说一定吓坏了。她当场就招了。她说，我从来不想去。是阿列克谢强迫我的。我跟他睡完全是在胁迫之下。

97
00:47:31.000 --> 00:48:03.000
a monastery. But of course, if Peter believes he was really the center of a conspiracy, then the implication is that the conspiracy would continue, that even if he's in a monastery, he will be the focus for plots and opposition. So for the time being, Peter keeps him under house arrest in St. Petersburg and all the time Alexis poor Alexis who's such a tragic figure and is so is so much his own worst advocate. He's begging and begging. Please. Can I see Afrosenia? You promised me that I could live with her I love her so much and
他总是向你抱怨个不停，总是发牢骚。他一直在向哈布斯堡皇帝批评你。每当他听到俄罗斯军队发生哗变或哗变传言时，阿列克谢都欣喜若狂。他经常谈论他当上沙皇之后要做什么。他说他会废除你所有的改革，他会抛弃圣彼得堡，他会把权力还给教会，他讨厌奴隶。他讨厌船只。他会放弃你所有的对外征服。彼得说，好吧，这就是证据。这不就来了。他命人把阿列克谢带进来。

98
00:48:03.000 --> 00:48:22.000
finally she is brought to the capital and questioned and it all goes horribly wrong for Alexis. Does she stand by him? She does not, Tom. She does not. She does not stand by her man. So in her luggage, Peter's agents find drafts of letters that Alexis had
阿弗罗西尼娅怎么样了？她根本没有受到惩罚，一点惩罚都没有。当阿列克谢被带进来时，他崩溃了。他精神彻底崩溃了。他对父亲说，是的，我确实就你写信给哈布斯堡皇帝。我确实说过你的坏话，但我当时喝醉了。是的，我确实谈过当我统治俄罗斯时我会做什么，但我从未密谋反对你，也没想过要杀死你。然后

99
00:48:22.000 --> 00:48:42.000
written to various kind of big wigs in Russia complaining about his treatment. And Peter has Afrosenia, he questions her personally, he has her brought to see him and he sits down and questions her, must have been terrifying for her. She cracked straight away. She said, I never wanted to go. Alexis forced me. I only slept with him under duress.
彼得说，那么，你听到叛乱和起义的传闻时幸灾乐祸这事怎么说？此时阿列克谢给出了一个精神错乱般自取灭亡的回答。他说，听到叛乱的传言我很兴奋，但我相信只有当你死了之后他们才会来找我，因为他们计划杀掉你。我并不相信他们会废黜你并让你活下去。但如果在你活着的时候他们找我，只要他们实力足够强大，我可能就会跟他们走。是的，这太疯了。

100
00:48:42.000 --> 00:49:12.000
He was always whining about you, always complaining. He was always criticizing you to the Habsburg emperor. Whenever he heard of a mutiny or rumors of mutinies in the Russian army, Alexis was delighted. He often talked about what he would do when he became Tsar. He said he'd scrap all your reforms, he would abandon St Petersburg, he'd give power back to the church, He hates slaves. He hates ships. He'd give away all your foreign conquests. And Peter says, well, this is the proof. Here we go. He has Alexis brought in.
这是一个语无伦次但又极度自证其罪的回答。于是阿列克谢被捕了，并被关押在彼得保罗要塞——正如你所说，汤姆，那是圣彼得堡的基石。他的作秀审判于6月14日开始。彼得再次亲自担任检察官。他说，阿列克谢作为阴谋的一部分逃往奥地利。

101
00:49:12.000 --> 00:49:34.000
What happens to Afrosenia? She's not punished at all, not punished at all. And when Alexis is brought in, he collapses. He has some kind of nervous breakdown. He says to his father, yes, I did write to the Habsburg emperor about you. I did speak ill of yousburg Emperor about you. I did speak ill of you, but only when I was drunk. Yes, I did talk about what I would do when I rule Russia, but I never plotted against you or meant to kill you. And then
他一直在与哈布斯堡皇帝密谋。他企图借助俄罗斯的哗变者、叛军以及外国军事援助来夺取王位。而且他对此一直在撒谎。当彼得陈述完案情后，阿列克谢并没有否认。他招认了。他招认了一个我不相信、而且我想没有任何历史学家会相信它曾经存在的阴谋。

102
00:49:34.000 --> 00:49:59.000
Peter says, well, what about this business about you rejoicing when you heard reports of mutinies and rebellions? And now Alexis gives a dementedly self-destructive answer. He says, I was excited at the talk of mutinies, but I believe they would only call for me when you were dead because they planned to kill you. I didn't believe they would dethrone you and let you live. But if they'd call me in your lifetime, probably I would have gone if they had been strong enough. Yeah, that is mad.
那他为什么要这么做？为什么人们在20世纪30年代会这么做？他们被打垮了，他们希望这是获得宽大处理的唯一途径，因为很显然法庭不会接受他无罪的辩解。所以最好的办法或许就是假装自己有罪并乞求宽恕。但彼得并没有原谅他。应彼得的要求，法庭下令进行进一步审讯。这意味着彼得的故事中在很多方面最黑暗的一章，我认为。

103
00:49:59.000 --> 00:50:22.000
It's a rambling but incredibly self-incriminating answer. So Alexis is arrested and he's imprisoned in the Peter and Paul fortress, which as you said, Tom, is the sort of foundation stone of St. Petersburg. And his show trial begins in June, 14th of June. And again, Peter acts as the prosecutor himself. He says, Alexis, he fled to Austria as part of a plot.
所以在6月19日，阿列克谢挨了25下九尾鞭。这通常足以致人死命。你知道的，你被这种巨型皮鞭抽打，背上的皮肉都被撕裂。五天后，他又挨了15下，他的背此时已经彻底毁了。只剩下一团血肉模糊的东西。现在他什么都招了。他告诉托尔斯泰伯爵，是的，我希望我父亲死。我本会花钱让奥地利人对他进行军事干预。于是在那个晚上，凭借这些口供，法庭判处他死刑。他们说他犯下了可怕的弑父大罪——首先是对国家之父的背叛，其次是对生身父亲的背叛——彼得所有的亲信和走狗都在这份判决书上签了名。

104
00:50:22.000 --> 00:50:43.000
He was plotting with the Habsburg emperor. He was intending to seize the throne with Russian mutineers and rebels and with foreign military aid. And he's been lying about it ever since. And when Peter has made the case, Alexis doesn't deny it. He confesses. He confesses to a conspiracy that I don't believe and I don't think any historian believes existed.
所以问题是，彼得会下令对自己的亲生儿子执行死刑吗？这个儿子其实内心深处什么坏事都没做。所有人都在等待结果揭晓。接着在6月26日星期二，圣彼得堡流言四起，传闻阿列克谢突发中风暴毙了。官方发布的说法是他是中风身亡的。彼得赶到他在监狱的病床前。阿列克谢做了彻底的忏悔。他痛改前非。父子二人相拥。

105
00:50:43.000 --> 00:51:11.000
So why is he doing that? Why did people do it in the 1930s? They're broken and they hope this is the only way to get clemency because it's very clear that the court will not accept his claim that he's not guilty. So maybe the best thing to do is to pretend that he is guilty and beg for forgiveness. But Peter doesn't forgive him. At Peter's request, the court orders further interrogation. And what this means is the darkest chapter of all in many ways in Peter's story, I think.
阿列克谢做了临终祈祷，事情就这样结束了。但实际上，这并不是事情的真相。我们从要塞的日志中了解到了真实发生的事情。实际上，那天清晨，彼得和他的亲信——包括托尔斯泰伯爵和亚历山大·缅什科夫——聚集在刑讯室里，把阿列克谢带到他们面前，对他折磨了三个小时。几个小时后，阿列克谢死了，

106
00:51:11.000 --> 00:51:58.000
So on the 19th of June, Alexis was given 25 lashes of the knout. That will often be enough to kill you. You know, you're beaten with this giant leather whip, chunks of flesh off your back. Five days later, he's given another 15 lashes and his back has now been completely destroyed. It's just a sort of mass of bleeding flesh. And now he's confessing to anything. He tells Count Tolstoy, yes, I wanted my father dead. I would have paid the Austrians to intervene militarily against him. And so that evening armed with that that the court sentences him to death. He's guilty they say of a horrid double patricide first against the father of his country and next against his father by nature and all of Peter's cronies and henchmen sign their names on this sentence.
实际上是被他亲生父亲活活拷打致死的。所以这简直是一个令人难以置信的恐怖故事。罗伯特·K·马西在他的传记《彼得大帝》中，将之与伊凡雷帝杀死自己的亲子进行了对比——这是俄罗斯历史上非常著名的一个场景。那是伊利亚·列宾创作的一幅非常著名的画作。不同之处在于，伊凡雷帝杀死自己的儿子是在暴怒之下动手，事后充满了杀害儿子的悔恨。但这里的严刑拷打是有预谋的。

107
00:51:58.000 --> 00:52:31.000
So the question is will Peter order the sentence against his own son who really deep down has done nothing wrong to be carried out. And everyone's waiting to find out the answer. And then on Tuesday the 26th of June, the rumours sweeps in Petersburg that Alexis has dropped dead of a stroke of some kind. And the story is given out that he had this stroke. Peter rushed to his bedside in the prison. Alexis made a full confession. He repented. Father and son embraced.
我的意思是，如果你想想那些酷刑、审讯、公开羞辱，这些已经持续了好几个星期，可以说也是长达多年的一种清算的一部分。但现在他们又折磨起他来，这个可怜的人背上的皮肉都被鞭笞得支离破碎，而他们还在对他施加天知道什么样的进一步酷刑。是的，很难想象会有父亲对自己的亲生骨肉做出这种事，但彼得的行为往往极其刷新人的想象力，我猜。是的。阿列克谢被举行了国葬，据报道彼得在葬礼上哭了。

108
00:52:31.000 --> 00:52:55.000
Alexis was given the last rites and that was the end of that. But actually, this isn't what happened. We know what happened from the logbook with the fortress. Actually, earlier that morning, Peter and his closest cronies, including Count Torstoy and including Alexander Menshikov, gathered in the torture chamber and had Alexis brought to them, and they worked on him for three hours. And a few hours later, Alexis died,
但我们也知道，那周他还去参加了大量的宴会和舞会，来庆祝波尔塔瓦战役的周年纪念，事后他还铸造了一枚奖章，仿佛是在庆祝一场伟大的胜利，奖章上刻着太阳冲破云层的图案，铭文写着：“天际已经放晴。”我的意思是，想象一下在自己亲生孩子死后做出这种事。我猜问题在于阿列克谢是名正言顺的继承人。那么现在王位继承怎么办？他有几个女儿，十几岁的女儿安娜和伊丽莎白，他还有阿列克谢的儿子彼得，只有三岁，但

109
00:52:55.000 --> 00:53:26.000
effectively having been tortured to death by his own father. So it's just an unbelievably horrifying story. And in his biography, Peter the Great, Robert K. Massey compares it with Ivan the Terrible killing his own son, which is a very famous scene in Russian history. It's a very famous painting by Ilya Repin. And the difference is that Ivan the Terrible killed his own son by lashing out against him in a fit of rage and then was full of remorse that he had killed his son. But the torture is kind of premeditated.
实际上她们都不太合适，所以他让他的妻子叶卡捷琳娜——也就是前玛尔塔·斯卡夫龙斯卡娅，那个快乐的女人——加冕为女皇，他为她举行了一场盛大的加冕典礼，这是在1724年，这显然是一个标志，表明她将成为他的继承人，这太不可思议了。我的意思是，她是一个目不识丁的立陶宛农家女，曾作为战俘来到俄罗斯，但这标志着彼得的绝对统治力和他的专制威权。是的。你知道的，这在1728年代他成长的时候是不可想象的。这也是他一生中在多大程度上改造了俄罗斯的一个衡量标准吧。

